some breaking news to bring you now from  uganda and there are reports that the  military have surrounded the home of the  main opposition candidate  in the country's elections ahead of  results uh being announced our africa  correspondent john sparks is on the  phone  for us john uh this is bobby wines house  yes that's right it's uh bobby wines  house uh  real name robert chagilani he has a  large house  located about an hour outside of the  capital  kampala and he sent out a couple of  panicky sounding tweets this afternoon  saying that  members of the military were encroaching  on his  property that his property had been  essentially surrounded by  the military we drove out there as  quickly as we could  and we found bobby wine  at the the edge of the the lawn which uh  there's been a gate and a fence and a  hill which leads down to  more of his property which is forested  we found him  uh somewhat anxiously examining the  property he told us that  he had seen troops soldiers  on the property that they had come and  beat one of his  guards up and we were introduced to the  guard who had  uh suffered some uh facial injuries and  then  he took us and a small number of other  journalists  on a tour of his property we went down a  hill  into some of the trees round the corner  and we saw a group of about  five uniformed men armed with  automatic weapons one of them picked up  his weapon  and uh pointed it at us and we  along with bobby wine ran for cover  i must say that at the stage was one of  the weapons discharged but it was  a frightening experience we ran back up  to the main  house had a chat with bobby wein he said  that this was an example of  the intimidation that he has faced  during the campaign  increasing intimidation now that the  election results  are expected they are expected to be  delivered by the  election commission tomorrow and he said  that the  government was putting him in his place  uh it's certainly an unusual highly  unusual way  to treat a presidential candidate uh in  this election or in any election he has  run a very strong campaign he has  fired up certainly younger members of  the electorate in this  uh country it does sound and look  like government intimidation to me  on another side of the property through  a chain link fence we could see  soldiers and plane clothes men with  armed weapons as well i tried to speak  to them  they said nothing it does look like a  clear attempt  at intimidation and  very uncomfortable position for for  bobby wine who is the  the country's best known most effective  opposition leader  it's very uncomfortable place for him to  be in at the moment
 

